# Spring Chicken Stew

Based on a Giant Grocery Catalog recipe, then merged with several others

{ rating="3" image="spring_chicken_stew.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 1 tsp [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" }
- [ ] 5 [carrots]{ ing="carrots" }, coined
- [ ] 1 large [yellow onion]{ ing="yellow-onion" }, 1/2” dice
- [ ] 5 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, minced
- [ ] 2 tsp [dried thyme]{ ing="dried-thyme" }
- [ ] 2 tsp [dried rosemary]{ ing="dried-rosemary" }
- [ ] 2 tsp [pepper]{ ing="pepper" }
- [ ] 2 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 1 cup [low-sodium chicken broth]{ ing="low-sodium-chicken-broth" }
- [ ] 1 [bay leaf]{ ing="bay-leaf" }
- [ ] 1 cup [white wine]{ ing="white-wine" } or 1 cup chicken broth
- [ ] 1.5 lb [golden or red potatoes]{ ing="golden-or-red-potatoes" }, quartered
- [ ] 1.5 lb [boneless skinless chicken thighs]{ ing="boneless-skinless-chicken-thighs" }
- [ ] bag of [frozen peas]{ ing="frozen-peas" }

## Recipe

1. Prep the [onion]{ ing="yellow-onion" } and [carrots]{ ing="carrots" } and quarter the [potatoes]{ ing="golden-or-red-potatoes" }
1. In an Instant Pot use the saute setting to brown the [onion]{ ing="yellow-onion" }, [carrots]{ ing="carrots" }, and [garlic]{ ing="garlic" } in a small amount of [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" }

   1. Add the spices for the last minute
1. To the pot, add the [chicken broth]{ ing="low-sodium-chicken-broth" } and/or [white wine]{ ing="white-wine" }, [potatoes]{ ing="golden-or-red-potatoes" }, and [bay leaf]{ ing="bay-leaf" }. Top with chicken.
1. Seal and set to high pressure. Cook for 13 minutes and natural release for 5 min
1. Open the pot and while on keep warm, remove the chicken, and add the [frozen peas]{ ing="frozen-peas" }
1. Shred and replace the chicken. Add [salt]{ ing="salt" } and [pepper]{ ing="pepper" } to taste. Serve once the [peas]{ ing="frozen-peas" } have heated

## Notes

1. For frozen boneless, skinless chicken thighs, put in without thawing. Keep potatoes whole and increase cook time to 20-25 min
1. To turn into Chicken Noodle Soup, replace the potatoes with 6 oz of Egg Noodles
